# github-projects (Cursor)

One shared board: Knitto SDLC (org knittotextile, #15).
Wave is the only sequencing field; Delivery Stage is legacy and hidden.
Full rules: `references/model.md`.

## Fields

Status (Backlog/Ready/In Progress/Done), Wave (Tracking, W0..Wn, mandatory),
Application (Studio/Atlas/Inspector/Cross-system, mandatory), Assignees
(issue assignees, mandatory; the old Owner text field is legacy), Estimate (hours), Target Date. Tracking = umbrella items.

## New work: lanjutan or new Wave

Never a loose item. Weigh with `references/lanjutan-vs-wave.md`:
lanjutan when same goal as an existing [Wn], <= 8h or <= 30% of that Wave,
one issue, no new app/major schema. Otherwise new Wave. Recommend one with
reasons, then let the user decide. No fitting parent: show candidates, ask.

## Issue

Title `[Wn] ...` or `[Wn-lanjutan] ...`.
Header: `Wave: Wn | Parent: o/r#n | Repo: o/r | Branch: feature/<slug> (from releases/staging) | Depends: ...`.
Sections: 1. Definition, 2. Changes, 3. Success Criteria (Functional, Test
mandatory, Regression checkboxes), optional 4. Keputusan terbuka.
Lanjutan = real GitHub sub-issue of its [Wn] parent. Done parent stays Done.
If Depends not Done, stay Backlog.

## Scripts (dry run unless --yes)

`node scripts/next-task.mjs`, `add-lanjutan.mjs --parent o/r#n --title ...`,
`set-fields.mjs o/r#n --wave W2 ...`, `set-status.mjs o/r#n "In Progress"`,
`mark-done.mjs o/r#n`, `lint-board.mjs`, `wave-report.mjs`.
See `scripts/README.md`.

## Views (manual, web UI, need approval)

All views grouped by Wave: All Work Items (table), Engineering Workflow
(board by Status, swimlanes Wave), Delivery Roadmap (Target Date),
Development Wave (table, `-wave:Tracking`).
See `references/views.md`.
